 the native path asks for 0.033 × tol.
 
+The pressure sub-solve's cap is the solver's own `fieldsplit_pressure_ksp_max_it`
+(default 200), read from the options database under the solver's prefix, so
+`stokes.petsc_options["fieldsplit_pressure_ksp_max_it"] = 1000` (or
+`-<prefix>fieldsplit_pressure_ksp_max_it 1000` on the command line) raises it on
+the rotated path as on the standard one. Raise it on P2/dP1 triangle meshes, where
+the Schur complement is poorly conditioned. The rotated Krylov solver is cached, so
+set the cap before the first solve. The velocity sub-solve's cap on this path stays
+200.
+
